<div id="logout">
  {{{card}}}
  <script>
    (async () => {
      try {
        const made = await fetch("/self-service/logout/browser", {
          credentials: "same-origin",
          headers: { Accept: "application/json" },
        });
        if (made.ok)
          await fetch((await made.json()).logout_url, {
            credentials: "same-origin",
            redirect: "manual",
          });
      } catch {}
      document.querySelector("#logout #accept")?.click();
    })();
  </script>
</div>
{{! The image's own logout.hbs, changed in what the question does. Hydra asks
    this page to confirm a sign-out and ends only its own session when the
    answer is Yes. The identity's session at this host is Kratos's, lasts as
    long as its lifespan, and answers the next sign-in's login challenge with
    no login page, so a person who signed out could not choose another method
    or account until it ran out. The script ends that session first and then
    presses the card's Yes, which is the answer to Hydra. A person who meets
    this page asked to be signed out, so the card's question is not put to
    them.

    THE SAME ORIGIN, because `/self-service` is routed to Kratos on this host
    and the session cookie is this host's. The logout flow is made with the
    cookie and answered as JSON, and the link it names is followed without
    taking its redirect: the cookie is cleared by the answer, and where the
    redirect leads is not needed.

    A FAILURE IS NOT A STOP. With no Kratos session the flow is refused, and
    the sign-out Hydra was asked for still has to be answered, so Yes is
    pressed either way. Under a content security policy that forbids inline
    script, or a browser that runs none, the card is the image's own and its
    Yes ends Hydra's session alone.

    READ AGAINST THE IMAGE
    sha256:46a7bac1ad0c67c692b37d0380613fd4618fd751afac2c5314aa8d3ae77ef1f0
    because the script presses the button by the id the image draws Yes
    with. Under an image that drew it otherwise the click finds nothing and
    the page waits for a person, still the image's own card. So
    tests/ory-ui-view.py holds ory-ui.yaml to that image and to the path it
    reads the view from. }}
